// RealityMargin · "What If Germany Never Invaded Russia?" The war model, version 3 (4 Nov 2026). Rules: sim/DESIGN_v3.md. Sources: 00_research/SOURCES.md and SOURCES2.md. Every odd explained: sim/INPUTS.md.
// One war = half-year turns, January 1941 to the end of 1949, from the real situation of December 1940: France fallen, Britain fighting, the USSR neutral and trading.
// THE PREMISE IS FORCED: Directive 21 is not signed, so there is no invasion in 1941. Nothing after that is forced. Hitler can still attack, Stalin can strike first, or neither.
// What viewers asked for (1,652 comments): "these are not independent events". So strength runs on real output figures, odds read the state of that war, each side has a strategy, leaders can fall, captured places can be lost again, and logistics are counted.
// No source gives any of these odds. They're our judgment, with what informed each one written down. roll(name, p) always draws one number, so pinning a turning point never shifts the rest of the stream.
// Usage: node run.mjs → results_v3.json + RESULTS_v3.md      Tests: node sim_test.mjs

